    "created_at": "2022-10-19T12:28:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-19T12:28:48Z",
    "body": "I think this is already covered:\r\n\r\n> The [width](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content-other.html#attr-dim-width) and [height](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content-other.html#attr-dim-height) attributes on an [img](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#the-img-element) element's [dimension attribute source](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#concept-img-dimension-attribute-source) [map to the dimension properties](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#maps-to-the-dimension-property) ['width'](https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/#the-width-property) and ['height'](https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/#the-height-property) on the [img](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#the-img-element) element respectively. They similarly [map to the aspect-ratio property (using dimension rules)](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#map-to-the-aspect-ratio-property-(using-dimension-rules)) of the [img](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#the-img-element) element.\r\n\r\nCoupled with:\r\n\r\n> When the text below says that a pair of attributes w and h on an element element map to the aspect-ratio property (using dimension rules), it means that if element has both attributes w and h, and parsing those attributes' values using the [rules for parsing dimension values](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/common-microsyntaxes.html#rules-for-parsing-dimension-values) doesn't generate an error or return a percentage for either, then the user agent is expected to use the parsed dimensions as a [presentational hint](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#presentational-hints) for the ['aspect-ratio'](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-sizing-4/#aspect-ratio) property of the form auto w / h.\r\n\r\nFor rendering of elements you always want to consult the Rendering section.\r\n\r\nLet me know if you have any remaining concerns.",
