    "updated_at": "2023-09-20T09:43:26Z",
    "body": "I believe this is already correctly handled in the spec. In the quoted text, note the definition of \"dimension attribute source\":\r\n\r\n> The [width](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content-other.html#attr-dim-width) and [height](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content-other.html#attr-dim-height) attributes on an [img](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#the-img-element) element's [dimension attribute source](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#concept-img-dimension-attribute-source) [map to the dimension properties](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#maps-to-the-dimension-property) ['width'](https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/#the-width-property) and ['height'](https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/#the-height-property) on the [img](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#the-img-element) element respectively. They similarly [map to the aspect-ratio property (using dimension rules)](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#map-to-the-aspect-ratio-property-(using-dimension-rules)) of the [img](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#the-img-element) element.\r\n\r\nIt is either a `source` element or the `img` element. If it's a `source` element, then `width`/`height` on `img` are *not* preshints.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
